{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall make the robe of the ephod.</b> This indicates that the robe was attached to the ephod, and so Rashi, of blessed memory, wrote, that the ephod was placed upon it like a belt." "<b>Entirely of tekhelet.</b> This teaches you that the robe was entirely tekhelet, containing no other color, and it was like our cloak, which has no opening for the head whose upper part was closed by sewing in front, and its neck opening was bound by the hole of the robe's mouth, and it had two wings in front which he would uncover and cover at will. And upon its hem all around were 72 pomegranates of tekhelet, argaman, and worm-scarlet — 36 on the side of the right wing and 36 on the side of the left wing — and the pomegranates were hollow, and inside them were 72 bells. And so the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded in Zevahim: they were 72 pairs, and inside them 72 clappers, and there were 36 on this side and 36 on that side. According to this, what is written ״פעמון זהב ורמון פעמון זהב ורמון״ — 'a golden bell and a pomegranate, a golden bell and a pomegranate' — is to be understood as within the pomegranate, that is, concealed inside it." "<b>But</b> Rashi, as well as (the Ramban) [the Rambam], of blessed memory, interpreted ״פעמון זהב ורמון״ — 'a golden bell and a pomegranate' — to mean that the bells were a single bell between two pomegranates, and so all of them upon the hem of the robe all around; but the bells were not actually inside the pomegranates, concealed within them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {2 "The printed text reads הרמב\"ן (Ramban) bracketed with הרמב\"ם (Rambam) as the corrected reading; the translation preserves both forms as found in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:15.250964430Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}